# Saved Replies: separate "access" from "create" — Show & Tell
#
# Feature: Roles & Permissions now splits Saved Replies into two permissions.
#   Access ON,  Create OFF -> view, search and insert existing Saved Replies only
#   Access ON,  Create ON  -> full access (create, edit, duplicate, delete)
#   Access OFF             -> no Saved Replies at all (Create is forced off)
# This flow shows the middle row: a member who can USE replies but not ADD them.
#
# Author it with:  "author a demo from input/saved-replies-create-permission.flow"
#
# ---- before the walk ---------------------------------------------------------
# * RUN THIS AGAINST A TEST ORGANIZATION, not a customer's. The flow SHOWS the
#   Member role settings but only CHANGES the demo member's own permissions.
# * Accounts (never in this file):
#     Admin / Owner   signs in with Google SSO. The target reuses the session in
#                     profile/, so sign in to app.salesmessage.com by hand in that
#                     profile once before the first take.
#     Member          signed in by hand once in profile-member/ (target
#                     salesmessage-member). No credentials are stored anywhere.
# * The org needs a few existing Saved Replies, at least one shared with
#   "Everyone", so the member has something to search and insert.
# * The member needs at least one conversation to open the reply picker in.
# * Afterwards, restore the role (Create back ON) off camera — see the last note.

name: saved-replies-create-permission
description: let members use existing Saved Replies without being able to create new ones
target: salesmessage
intro: Saved Replies permissions | Let your team use replies without adding new ones
outro: Thanks for watching | Questions? Reach out any time - we are happy to help

Steps:

# -- as the Admin / Owner (already signed in by the target) --
Open Settings, then Role & Permissions
Scroll to the Saved Replies sections
Confirm Saved Replies now has two separate sections: "Saved Replies management" (Can create Saved Replies) and "Saved Replies access" (Can access Saved Replies), each with Admin / Manager / Member / Observer columns
Hover the Member checkbox under "Can access Saved Replies": confirm the tooltip "Also removes Create access"
# The same two settings exist per member and override the role. Restrict ONE member,
# so nobody else in the org is affected:
Open Settings, then Members
Hover the info icon on Demo Demo's role badge: confirm the tooltip "Custom permissions"
Open Demo Demo's "..." menu, then User profile, then the Permissions tab
Confirm the same two sections appear for this one member
Make sure "Can access Saved Replies" is ON
Turn "Can create Saved Replies" OFF
Click Save in the Cancel / Save bar that appears at the bottom once a box changes
Confirm the member now reads Access ON, Create OFF
# Walk notes (2026-10-17): Member checkboxes are #cannedMessagemembercheckbox (create)
# and #cannedMessageAccessmembercheckbox (access). Observer's create box shows
# "Can't be applied to this role"; "Requires Saved Replies access" only appears on
# a role allowed Saved Replies whose Access is off. Changes are NOT saved until
# Save is clicked (the bar disappears ~0.2s later; no toast). Page load ~4.5-7.5s.
# A member with "Custom permissions" (info icon on the role badge) ignores the role
# setting — their own page at /settings/members/<id>/permissions wins. There the
# checkboxes are #cannedMessage (create) and #cannedMessageAccess (access).

# -- switch to the member --
# Recorded as a SEPARATE take from a second Chrome profile (profile-member/,
# target salesmessage-member) and joined after part 1. Signing in on camera hit a
# 2FA enrolment dialog and a reCAPTCHA, and would show the member's email.
Cut to the member's Conversations page

# -- member: Saved Replies inside a conversation --
# The member's inbox has no conversations, and texting is not enabled on it, so use
# the New message composer: nothing can be sent from it by accident.
Dismiss the "Welcome to Salesmsg" chat popup if it is showing
Click New message
Open the Saved Replies picker: the bookmark icon in the composer toolbar (tooltip "Saved replies /")
Confirm the member can see and search the existing Saved Replies, including ones shared with Everyone
Search for an existing reply
Pause on the result list
Hover Create: confirm it is disabled with a tooltip
Confirm Duplicate and Manage are disabled, and Edit and Delete are not shown
Insert an existing Saved Reply into the composer
Confirm the reply text appears in the message box — do NOT send it

# -- member: the Saved Replies settings page --
Open Settings, then Saved Replies
Confirm the member sees the existing Saved Replies list
Hover Create: confirm it is disabled with a tooltip
Confirm Duplicate is disabled, and Edit and Delete are not shown on any reply
Pause on the list: use is allowed, adding and changing replies is not

# ---- after the take (off camera, not part of the video) ----------------------
# Sign back in as the admin and turn "Can create Saved Replies" back ON on Demo Demo's
# own Permissions page, so the account returns to Access ON, Create ON.
